## P-009 PATCH PACKET — MCP INTENT COMPILER LAYER (PRODUCTION SPEC)

### Patch ID

**P-009-MCP-INTENT-COMPILER-LAYER**

---

# 1. OBJECTIVE

Introduce a **single MCP-side compilation layer** that converts:

> natural intent → optimized execution packet → connector-ready request

This eliminates:

* tool chaining
* repeated querying
* multi-step MCP orchestration overhead
* fragmented retrieval logic

---

# 2. CORE PRINCIPLE

> MCP does not execute intelligence. It compiles intent into minimal deterministic actions.

---

# 3. SYSTEM POSITION (CRITICAL)

### BEFORE (wrong model)

```text id="x91kq1"
JARVIS → GOD SYSTEMS → MCP → tools → connectors
```

### AFTER (P-009)

```text id="mcp009"
JARVIS → GOD SYSTEMS (evaluation only)
       → MCP INTENT COMPILER (P-009)
       → CONNECTOR CORE (P-008)
       → Supabase / GitHub
```

---

# 4. NEW MODULE: INTENT COMPILER

## Name:

**MCP Intent Compiler (MIC)**

---

## Responsibilities

### 1. Intent normalization

* convert raw requests into structured intent objects

### 2. Query minimization

* collapse multiple tool calls into single batched requests

### 3. retrieval planning (NOT execution)

* decide *what must be fetched together*

### 4. payload construction

* build connector-ready request

---

## Explicit NON-RESPONSIBILITIES

MIC does NOT:

* decide governance (AEGIS owns this)
* route meaning (ODIN is deprecated for runtime routing)
* execute writes (CONNECTOR CORE does)
* store memory (MNEMOS does)

---

# 5. CORE DATA STRUCTURE

```ts id="p9core01"
type compiled_intent_packet = {
  trace_id: string

  intent: string

  mode: "retrieve" | "write" | "sync" | "observe"

  targets: string[]

  operations: {
    supabase?: any
    github?: any
    mcp?: any
  }

  compression_level: "low" | "medium" | "high"

  dependency_graph: string[]

  metadata: {
    source: "JARVIS" | "AYRE"
    optimization_score: number
  }

  timestamp: string
}
```

---

# 6. COMPILATION RULES

## Rule A — Multi-call collapse

If more than 1 tool is needed → MUST merge into single packet.

---

## Rule B — No sequential MCP calls

MIC outputs ONE structured request per intent cycle.

---

## Rule C — Dependency flattening

All tool dependencies must be expressed as:

```text id="flatdep"
dependency_graph[]
```

NOT runtime chaining.

---

## Rule D — Connector-ready output only

MIC output is FINAL before execution.

No downstream interpretation allowed.

---

# 7. INTENT CLASSIFICATION LAYERS

MIC must classify into:

| Intent   | Behavior                    |
| -------- | --------------------------- |
| retrieve | batch reads across systems  |
| write    | single unified write packet |
| sync     | GitHub + Supabase alignment |
| observe  | telemetry + state snapshot  |

---

# 8. TOOL COLLAPSE MODEL (KEY OPTIMIZATION)

### BEFORE:

* jarvis_recall
* jarvis_query
* jarvis_event
* jarvis_status

### AFTER:

```text id="collapse1"
1 compiled_intent_packet → MCP → result
```

MIC replaces all intermediate orchestration.

---

# 9. MCP ROLE REDUCTION (IMPORTANT)

MCP is now split into:

## A. MIC (P-009)

* compiles intent
* optimizes calls
* builds execution packets

## B. CONNECTOR CORE (P-008)

* executes packet
* writes to Supabase/GitHub
* emits trace

---

# 10. PERFORMANCE MODEL

## Before:

* 3–12 tool calls per intent

## After:

* 1 compile step
* 1 execution step
* 1 trace emission

---

